+/*
+ * 6.18 port. The vendor did:
+ *     release_reset(SF_CATIP_SOFT_RESET)       - ungate every clock, deassert
+ *                                                reset, enable bus output
+ *     clk_gate &= 0xFE                         - then switch bit 0 back off
+ * Bit 0 of that gate register is the DFT clock; bits 1..3 are axi, boot and lp.
+ * The mainline DTS models the same registers as rfrst (reset-controller) and
+ * rfclk (periph-clk, which writes both the gate and the BOE register), and the
+ * wlan_rf node deliberately takes only <&rfclk 1>, <&rfclk 2>, <&rfclk 3> -
+ * axi, boot, lp - leaving the DFT clock off. So this is the same end state.
+ *
+ * The vendor also cleared the block's MEMCTL register (soft_reset + 0x14) to
+ * lift internal memory shutdown. Mainline models no such register, and on this
+ * board it reads 0 from reset (measured on the running v2.0 image at
+ * 0x19e08814, and the same for both WiFi blocks), so there is nothing to lift.
+ */
+/* startcore/sf_reset_compat.c - the vendor's arch reset helpers, reproduced */
